{
  "version": 1,
  "readme": [
    "demo — the starter session: a generated drum kit under two tape pads, at",
    "78bpm in A minor. A combination of the euclid-ghosts and ambient-tape",
    "sessions, and a tour of the three ways sound gets scheduled in ribbit.",
    "",
    "  1. authored     lead — four events written into the file by hand.",
    "                  /lead events lists them, remove_event=<n> prunes one.",
    "  2. derived      grid + ghosts — two drum generators deriving a rhythm",
    "                  from rules, patched into the four percussion tracks.",
    "  3. varied       chords + shimmer — a hand-written pattern from the",
    "                  ambientchords pack, seeded variations generated on it.",
    "",
    "Nothing here replaces anything: generated notes run alongside a track's",
    "own authored events, and several generators can feed one track.",
    "",
    "  kick snare hats percs   percsampler, one drum category each",
    "  pad                     tapepad — the chords, mid register",
    "  haze                    tapepad — a slower, dirtier layer an octave up",
    "  lead                    oscsynth — the four authored notes",
    "  verb  echo              reverb and dotted-eighth delay buses",
    "",
    "The drum half:",
    "",
    "  grid    euclidpercs — the skeleton. Identical every pass; this is the",
    "          thing you can count against.",
    "  ghosts  markovpercs — the decoration. Quiet and off the beat, patched to",
    "          snare/hats/percs only, never the kick. Because each track loads",
    "          only its own category, a ghost hit for a category a track doesn't",
    "          own is simply silent. No filtering, just routing.",
    "",
    "Try:",
    "  /start                     turn the engine on (nothing sounds until you do)",
    "  /grid                      the fixed skeleton",
    "  /ghosts                    the decoration, as a step string",
    "  /ghosts seed=random        re-roll the decoration; the grid holds",
    "  /grid dropout=0.4 8b       thin the skeleton, let the ghosts through",
    "  /grid preset=fourfloor at=cycle    swap the backbone on the next bar",
    "  /pad cutoff=400 16b        close the pad right down — the sub stays",
    "  /pad wow=60 8b             warp the tape, slowly",
    "  /haze hiss=0.6             tape noise as an instrument",
    "  /chords variation=0.7      revoice the progression",
    "  /chords pattern=tidal      a different one from the same pack",
    "  /lead waveform=square      swap the oscillator",
    "  /lead events               list the authored notes",
    "  /harmony root=53           move every pitched track to F",
    "  /clock bpm=96 8            ramp the tempo over 8 seconds",
    "  /pad random                re-roll every randomizable param at once",
    "  /pad sat.r=false           leave one out of the next bulk re-roll",
    "",
    "Add at=beat or at=cycle to any command to land it on the next boundary.",
    "",
    "Scenes are made live rather than shipped in the file:",
    "  /save quiet                snapshot the whole mix under a name",
    "  /kick gain=0.1  /pad gain=0.9      wreck it",
    "  /recall quiet 8b           ramp everything back over 8 beats",
    "",
    "Two LFOs, showing both kinds of patch:",
    "  drift -> ghosts.velocity   a generator param, read once per note",
    "  sweep -> pad.cutoff        a synth param, so each chord enters at a",
    "                             different brightness",
    "",
    "master runs a goodenizer called 'glue' — compressor, saturator, tilt EQ",
    "and limiter in one box. /glue shows how hard it's working, /glue mix=0",
    "takes it off. The goodenizer-demo session tours it in full; chorale-drift",
    "is the same pad idea with no rhythm at all."
  ],
